            "name": "db-migration-playbook.md",
            "content": "---\nproject: mbl\ntype: db-migration-playbook\ndocument_id: DBMIG-MBL-7.0\nversion: \"7.0\"\ndate: 2026-05-25\nstandard: Evo Trident 00-06\nai_context: true\n---\n\n# Database Migration Playbook — MBL Sales Platform\n\n> Quy trình thực hiện DB migration an toàn cho 9 PostgreSQL databases\n> Bao gồm: schema changes, data migration, rollback strategy\n\n---\n\n## 1. Migration Strategy\n\n### 1.1 Tooling\n\n| Tool | Purpose | Environment |\n|------|---------|:-----------:|\n| **Flyway** | Schema versioning + migration | All |\n| **pg_dump / pg_restore** | Full backup/restore | All |\n| **pgAdmin** | Manual inspection | Dev/Staging |\n| **Liquibase** (alternative) | Change tracking | Future option |\n\n### 1.2 Naming Convention\n\n```\nV{version}__{description}.sql\nExample: V7.001__add_per_collection_kpi_table.sql\n         V7.002__alter_lead_add_persona_column.sql\n         V7.003__insert_master_data_persona.sql\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Pre-Migration Checklist\n\n```markdown\n- [ ] Migration SQL reviewed by Tech Lead\n- [ ] Migration tested on Dev → Staging (same data volume)\n- [ ] Backup taken: `pg_dump -Fc {db} > backup_{db}_{date}.dump`\n- [ ] Rollback script prepared and tested\n- [ ] Affected services identified (see Service-DB Map below)\n- [ ] Maintenance window communicated (if needed)\n- [ ] Monitoring dashboards open\n- [ ] On-call team notified\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Service ↔ Database Map\n\n| Service | Database | Tables Count | Est. Size | Migration Risk |\n|---------|----------|:------------:|:---------:|:--------------:|\n| M01-Auth | app4sale_auth_service | 5 | Small (<1GB) | 🟢 Low |\n| M02-Lead | app4sale_lead_management_service | 6 | Medium (5GB) | 🟡 Medium |\n| M03-CRM | app4sale_crm_service | 8 | Large (20GB) | 🟡 Medium |\n| M04-Performance | app4sale_performance_service | 10 | Large (15GB) | 🔴 High |\n| M05-Contest | app4sale_contest_service | 4 | Small (<1GB) | 🟢 Low |\n| M06-Sales | app4sale_sales_service | 7 | Large (10GB) | 🔴 High |\n| M07-Training | app4sale_training_service | 3 | Small (<1GB) | 🟢 Low |\n| M08-Policy | app4sale_policy_service | 8 | Large (25GB) | 🔴 High |\n| M09-Notification | app4sale_notification_service | 4 | Medium (3GB) | 🟢 Low |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Migration Types & Procedures\n\n### Type A: Non-Breaking (Zero Downtime)\n\n> ADD column (nullable), ADD index, ADD table, INSERT master data\n\n```bash\n# 1. Deploy migration\nflyway -url=jdbc:postgresql://host/db migrate\n\n# 2. Verify\nflyway info\n\n# 3. No service restart needed\n# New columns are nullable — app code handles gracefully\n```\n\n### Type B: Breaking Schema Change (Requires Downtime)\n\n> DROP column, RENAME column, ALTER column type, ADD NOT NULL\n\n```bash\n# 1. Announce maintenance window\n# 2. Scale down service replicas to 0\nkubectl scale deployment m06-sales --replicas=0\n\n# 3. Take backup\npg_dump -Fc app4sale_sales_service > backup_m06_$(date +%Y%m%d).dump\n\n# 4. Apply migration\nflyway migrate\n\n# 5. Verify schema\npsql -c \"\\d+ table_name\"\n\n# 6. Scale up\nkubectl scale deployment m06-sales --replicas=3\n\n# 7. Smoke test\ncurl -f https://api.mbl.internal/m06/health\n```\n\n### Type C: Data Migration (Large Volume)\n\n> Backfill data, transform existing records\n\n```bash\n# 1. Run in batches (10K records per batch)\n# 2. Use CONCURRENTLY for index creation\nCREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY idx_new ON table(column);\n\n# 3. Monitor progress\nSELECT count(*) FROM table WHERE new_column IS NOT NULL;\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Rollback Procedures\n\n### 5.1 Schema Rollback\n\n```bash\n# Option A: Flyway undo (if undo scripts prepared)\nflyway -url=jdbc:postgresql://host/db undo\n\n# Option B: Manual rollback script\npsql -f rollback_V7.001.sql\n\n# Option C: Full restore from backup\npg_restore -d app4sale_sales_service backup_m06_20260525.dump\n```\n\n### 5.2 Rollback Decision Matrix\n\n| Scenario | Action | Max Recovery Time |\n|----------|--------|:-----------------:|\n| Migration script error | Fix script, re-run | 10 min |\n| Data corruption detected | Restore from backup | 30 min |\n| Performance degradation | Roll back schema + reindex | 1h |\n| Full disaster | Restore from backup | 2h |\n\n---\n\n## 6. Environment-Specific Configuration\n\n| Config | Dev | Staging | Production |\n|--------|-----|---------|:----------:|\n| Max connections | 20 | 50 | 200 |\n| Shared buffers | 256MB | 1GB | 4GB |\n| Work mem | 64MB | 256MB | 1GB |\n| WAL level | minimal | replica | replica |\n| Auto-vacuum | ON | ON | ON (tuned) |\n| Backup frequency | None | Daily | Every 6h |\n| Backup retention | — | 7 days | 30 days |\n| Point-in-time recovery | — | — | ✅ Enabled |\n\n---\n\n## 7. Post-Migration Verification\n\n```markdown\n- [ ] Schema matches expected state (`flyway info` shows \"Success\")\n- [ ] Record counts match pre-migration (±0.01% tolerance)\n- [ ] Application health checks pass (`/actuator/health`)\n- [ ] Key API endpoints return 200 (smoke test)\n- [ ] ETL pipeline runs successfully (next scheduled cycle)\n- [ ] Monitoring: no error spike in last 30 minutes\n- [ ] Performance: API p99 latency within SLA\n```\n\n---\n\n*DB Migration Playbook MBL v7.0 | 2026-05-25*\n",
