            "content": "---\nproject: mbl\ntype: sla\ndocument_id: SLA-MBL-6.3\nversion: \"6.3\"\ndate: 2026-05-12\nstandard: Evo Trident 00-06\nai_context: true\napplies_to: all_modules\nrelated_docs:\n  - \"NFR-MBL-6.3 (nfr.md)\"\n  - \"DR-MBL-6.3 (disaster-recovery.md)\"\n---\n\n# Service Level Agreements (SLA) — MBL Platform\n\n> **Version:** 6.3 | **Updated:** 2026-05-12\n> **Scope:** Internal SLA giữa IT Development ↔ Business Operations ↔ Vendor Partners\n> **Review Cycle:** Semi-annual (next review: 2026-11-12)\n\n---\n\n## 1. Service Availability SLA\n\n### 1.1 Platform Availability\n\n| Service | Target Uptime | Max Downtime/Month | Measurement |\n|---------|:-------------:|:------------------:|-------------|\n| M-Bro Mobile App (API) | 99.9% | 43 min | Prometheus uptime probe |\n| Admin Web Portal | 99.5% | 3.6 hours | Synthetic monitoring |\n| eBao Integration (DP) | 99.5% | 3.6 hours | eBao callback success rate |\n| Push Notification (Firebase) | 99.0% | 7.2 hours | Firebase delivery report |\n| Kafka Event Pipeline | 99.9% | 43 min | Consumer lag monitoring |\n\n### 1.2 Planned Maintenance Windows\n\n| Window | Schedule | Duration | Notification |\n|--------|----------|:--------:|:------------:|\n| Weekly maintenance | Sunday 02:00–06:00 (UTC+7) | ≤ 4 hours | 24h advance |\n| Emergency patch | Anytime (P1 only) | ≤ 2 hours | Immediate |\n| Major upgrade | Scheduled (monthly) | ≤ 6 hours | 72h advance |\n\n> **Note:** Planned maintenance windows are excluded from uptime calculation.\n\n---\n\n## 2. API Performance SLA\n\n### 2.1 Response Time Targets\n\n| API Category | P50 | P95 | P99 | Measurement Window |\n|-------------|:---:|:---:|:---:|:------------------:|\n| Authentication (`/auth/*`) | < 200ms | < 500ms | < 1s | Rolling 5 min |\n| Read operations (`GET /*`) | < 300ms | < 500ms | < 1.5s | Rolling 5 min |\n| Write operations (`POST/PUT /*`) | < 500ms | < 1s | < 2s | Rolling 5 min |\n| Heavy operations (import/export) | < 2s | < 5s | < 10s | Per request |\n| External integration (eBao) | < 3s | < 5s | < 15s | Per request |\n\n### 2.2 Error Rate Targets\n\n| Metric | Target | Alert Threshold | Escalation |\n|--------|:------:|:---------------:|------------|\n| API 5xx rate | < 0.5% | > 1% for 5 min | P2 — Slack alert |\n| API 4xx rate | < 5% | > 10% for 10 min | P3 — Investigate |\n| Kafka processing failure | < 0.1% | > 0.5% | P2 — DLQ review |\n| Database connection failure | 0% | Any failure | P2 — Immediate |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Support SLA\n\n### 3.1 Incident Response Times\n\n| Severity | First Response | Resolution Target | Escalation After |\n|:--------:|:--------------:|:-----------------:|:----------------:|\n| **P1 Critical** | < 15 min | < 1 hour | 30 min |\n| **P2 High** | < 30 min | < 4 hours | 2 hours |\n| **P3 Medium** | < 2 hours | < 1 business day | 4 hours |\n| **P4 Low** | < 8 hours | < 5 business days | 2 business days |\n\n### 3.2 Incident Definitions\n\n| Severity | Definition | Examples |\n|:--------:|------------|----------|\n| P1 | Platform completely unavailable, data loss risk | Full outage, DB corruption, security breach |\n| P2 | Major feature degraded, workaround not available | e-App submission failing, policy query down |\n| P3 | Feature impacted, workaround available | Export slow, notifications delayed |\n| P4 | Minor issue, cosmetic, enhancement request | UI typo, report formatting, feature request |\n\n### 3.3 Business Hours\n\n| Metric | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Support hours** | Mon–Fri 08:00–18:00 (UTC+7) |\n| **On-call hours** | 24/7 for P1/P2 |\n| **Holiday schedule** | Vietnamese public holidays |\n| **Escalation contact** | Slack #mbl-ops → Phone for P1 |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Vendor SLA\n\n### 4.1 Development Vendor SLAs\n\n| Vendor | Scope | Response SLA | Delivery SLA | Penalty |\n|--------|-------|:------------:|:------------:|---------|\n| **Evotek** | FE + BE (Agency/Bancas) | < 4h (P2) | Sprint commitment 90% | Contract clause |\n| **GTS** | FE (Dashboard, LDP) | < 8h | Sprint commitment 85% | Contract clause |\n| **VTI** | DP Backend services | < 2h (P1) | Sprint commitment 90% | Contract clause |\n| **eBao** | Core Insurance API | < 4h | Per SLA agreement | — |\n\n### 4.2 External Service SLAs\n\n| Service | Provider | Uptime SLA | Response SLA | Fallback |\n|---------|----------|:----------:|:------------:|----------|\n| Core Insurance | eBao PAS | 99.5% | < 4h | Circuit breaker + Kafka queue |\n| Payment Gateway | VNPAY | 99.9% | < 1h | Bank transfer fallback |\n| eKYC | Vendor (NDA) | 99.0% | < 8h | Manual KYC process |\n| Push Notification | Firebase | 99.95% | N/A (managed) | SMS fallback |\n| CRM Webhook | MB Bank CRM | 99.0% | < 24h | Manual lead import |\n| Survey | Filum | 99.0% | < 24h | Survey disabled gracefully |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Data SLA\n\n### 5.1 Data Freshness\n\n| Data Type | Source | Freshness Target | Sync Mechanism |\n|-----------|--------|:----------------:|----------------|\n| Lead data (CRM-MB) | CRM webhook | Near real-time (< 5 min) | Kafka event |\n| Policy status | eBao callback | < 15 min | Kafka + polling |\n| Premium collection | eBao billing | Daily batch (02:00) | ETL job |\n| KPI/Commission | eBao + internal calc | Daily refresh (04:00) | ETL + cache |\n| Customer profile | DP partner-service | Real-time (on-demand) | API call |\n| Team structure | HR System | Daily sync (06:00) | Scheduled job |\n\n### 5.2 Backup & Retention SLA\n\n| Data | Backup Frequency | Retention | Recovery SLA |\n|------|:----------------:|:---------:|:------------:|\n| PostgreSQL (full) | Daily 02:00 | 30 days | < 30 min |\n| PostgreSQL (WAL) | Continuous (5-min) | 7 days | < 15 min (PITR) |\n| eKYC documents | Real-time (S3) | 5 years | < 1 hour |\n| Voice recordings | Real-time (S3) | 5 years | < 1 hour |\n| Audit logs | Continuous | 5 years | < 24 hours |\n| Kafka events | Continuous | 7 days | Topic replay |\n\n---\n\n## 6. Capacity SLA\n\n### 6.1 Auto-Scaling Triggers\n\n| Resource | Metric | Scale-Up Trigger | Scale-Down Trigger | Max |\n|----------|--------|:----------------:|:------------------:|:---:|\n| BFF Pods | CPU usage | > 70% for 3 min | < 30% for 10 min | 4 |\n| DP Pods | CPU usage | > 70% for 3 min | < 30% for 10 min | 3 |\n| DB Connections | Pool utilization | > 80% | N/A (manual) | 100 |\n\n### 6.2 Storage Capacity\n\n| Storage | Current Usage | Alert Threshold | Max Capacity |\n|---------|:------------:|:---------------:|:------------:|\n| PostgreSQL | ~20 GB | 80% (160 GB) | 200 GB |\n| S3 (documents) | ~100 GB | 80% (800 GB) | 1 TB |\n| Redis cache | ~2 GB | 80% (6.4 GB) | 8 GB |\n| Kafka logs | ~50 GB | 80% (80 GB) | 100 GB |\n\n---\n\n## 7. SLA Reporting\n\n### 7.1 Monthly SLA Report\n\n```yaml\nmonthly_report_template:\n  period: \"YYYY-MM\"\n  sections:\n    availability:\n      - \"Uptime percentage per service\"\n      - \"Number and duration of outages\"\n      - \"Planned vs unplanned downtime\"\n    \n    performance:\n      - \"P95 latency trend\"\n      - \"Error rate trend\"\n      - \"Throughput (requests/day)\"\n    \n    incidents:\n      - \"P1/P2 incidents count\"\n      - \"Mean Time To Detect (MTTD)\"\n      - \"Mean Time To Resolve (MTTR)\"\n    \n    capacity:\n      - \"Storage growth rate\"\n      - \"User growth rate\"\n      - \"Scale events count\"\n```\n\n### 7.2 SLA Breach Procedure\n\n| Step | Action | Timeline |\n|:----:|--------|:--------:|\n| 1 | Detect SLA breach (automated alert) | Immediate |\n| 2 | Root cause analysis | < 24 hours |\n| 3 | Report to stakeholders | < 48 hours |\n| 4 | Corrective action plan | < 1 week |\n| 5 | Implement fix | Per severity |\n| 6 | Verify SLA restored | Next reporting period |\n\n---\n\n*SLA v6.3 | 2026-05-12 | Service Level Agreements for MBL Platform | Evo Trident Standard*\n",
